# {{.ExportedName}}

A go-sicky service project generated by `sicky new --type {{.Type}}`.

## Getting Started

```bash
make build   # runs `go mod tidy`, then compiles ./bin/svc
./bin/svc
```

The scaffold itself never touches the network: the first `make build` (or
`make deps`, which runs `go mod tidy`) downloads the dependencies the project
imports.

{{if or .WithFiber .WithHTTP}}Verify a running HTTP stack:

```bash
{{if .WithHTTP}}curl localhost:9980/ping   # net/http (bunrouter)
{{end}}{{if .WithFiber}}curl localhost:3000/ping   # fiber
{{end}}```

{{end}}## Configuration

Edit `config.json` to change server addresses and framework options:

{{if .WithHTTP}}- net/http server listens on `:9980` (bunrouter)
{{end}}{{if .WithFiber}}- Fiber server listens on `:3000` (fasthttp)
{{end}}{{if .WithGRPC}}- gRPC server listens on `:44945`
{{end}}- Manager endpoints listen on `127.0.0.1:8888` (loopback by default): `/metrics`, `/health`, `/ready`, `/live`

{{if and (eq .Type "standard") .WithHTTP .WithAuth}}### Application credentials

The generated `app` block ships empty credentials, and the scaffold never
generates a default login:

```json
"app": {
    "admin_username": "",
    "admin_password": "",
    "general_token": ""
}
```

`POST /auth/login` answers 401 until `app.admin_username` and
`app.admin_password` are both set. `app.general_token` is an alternative bearer
token accepted by `validateSession`; leave it empty to disable that path.
Never commit real credentials.

{{end}}{{if .Models}}### Database

`--model` is what enables bun and the database connection. `config.json`
carries a placeholder DSN that must be replaced before the service starts:

```json
"sicky": {
    "infra": {
        "bun": {
            "driver": "postgres",
            "dsn": "postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/{{.Name}}?sslmode=disable"
        }
    }
}
```

`--initdb` creates the PostgreSQL `uuid-ossp` extension and every generated
model's table, then exits without serving:

```bash
./bin/svc --initdb
```

Generated models use the standard library `uuid` package and default their
`id` column to `uuid_generate_v4()`. That function is part of PostgreSQL's
`uuid-ossp` extension; on any other driver remove
`default:uuid_generate_v4()` from the model's `ID` field. `Create` assigns an
ID in Go when it is nil.

{{end}}## Adding a Resource

{{if eq .Type "standard"}}One command generates the model, service, HTTP handler and its request/response
DTOs, and wires them into `config.json` and `main.go`:

```bash
sicky generate model <name>
```

The wiring adds `sicky.infra.bun`, `MustInfra`, the `--initdb` flag, the
`InitDB` calls and the handler registration. Pass `--no-wire` to write only the
files; re-running against an existing resource fails before writing anything
unless `--force` is given.
{{else}}Handlers live in `handler/`. Add one with:

```bash
sicky generate handler <name> --type {{if .WithFiber}}fiber{{else}}http{{end}}
```
{{end}}
{{if eq .Type "mcp"}}## MCP Configuration

For MCP-type services over stdio:

```json
{
    "mcpServers": {
        "{{.Name}}": {
            "command": "./bin/svc"
        }
    }
}
```

{{end}}## Docker

Plain tags resolve to docker.io by default (no registry prefix).
Retag explicitly for a private registry.

```bash
make docker
make push
```

## Project Structure

```
{{.Name}}/
  main.go                  # Entry point: sicky.Init, servers, service
  config.go                # Root configuration (server, service, sicky{{if eq .Type "standard"}}, app{{end}})
  config.json              # Default runtime configuration
{{if eq .Type "standard"}}  app/                     # Application-level configuration
    config.go
{{if .WithAuth}}    session.go             # In-memory access-token sessions
{{end}}{{if or .WithHTTP .WithFiber .WithGRPC}}  handler/
{{if .WithHTTP}}    http.go                # ping{{if .WithAuth}} and the auth middleware{{end}}
{{if .WithAuth}}    auth.http.go           # login / logout
{{end}}    request/http.go        # Request DTOs
    response/http.go       # Response codes, messages and DTOs
{{if .Models}}    <resource>.http.go     # CRUD routes
{{end}}{{end}}{{if .WithFiber}}    fiber.go
{{end}}{{if .WithGRPC}}    grpc.go
{{end}}{{end}}{{if or .Models (and .WithHTTP .WithAuth)}}  service/                 # Business layer
{{if and .WithHTTP .WithAuth}}    auth.go
{{end}}{{if .Models}}    <resource>.go
{{end}}{{end}}{{if .Models}}  model/                   # bun models
    <resource>.go
{{end}}{{else}}  handler/
    handler.go
{{if .WithFiber}}    fiber.go
{{end}}{{if .WithHTTP}}    http.go
{{end}}{{end}}  Makefile
  Dockerfile
  README.md
{{if eq .Type "standard"}}  AGENTS.md
{{end}}  go.mod
```
